# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BCAiRouter — environment variables (local)
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local open mode: leave every auth variable below empty → no login; every page
# and API is open on this machine and treated as the owner. Never expose it.
#
# Server mode: setting AUTH_OWNER_EMAIL (or GATEWAY_API_KEY / ADMIN_PASSWORD)
# turns on default-deny auth: only /, /login, /api/auth/*, /api/public/* and
# /api/health stay public; /v1/* needs a bcai_live_* key issued at /admin/keys;
# everything else is owner-only. Production setup: .env.production.example.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── Owner (server mode) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google account(s) allowed to sign in — comma / semicolon / whitespace separated.
AUTH_OWNER_EMAIL=

# Google OAuth — the owner's web login.
# Create a "Web application" client at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   Authorized redirect URI: {NEXTAUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/google
# NEXTAUTH_URL=https://your-domain.example.com
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET=<generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))">
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ─── Optional owner access (not used in production) ─────────────────────
# Master Bearer key with owner rights on /v1/* and /api/*.
# GATEWAY_API_KEY=
# Password login: offered on /login only while Google OAuth is not configured.
# Signed httpOnly cookie (7 days); 5 wrong attempts per IP / 15 min → 429.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# HMAC key for that cookie (falls back to ADMIN_PASSWORD).
# ADMIN_COOKIE_SECRET=

# ─── Secrets at rest ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provider API keys are entered at /setup and stored in the DB, not in env.
# This key encrypts them (AES-256-GCM).
# APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ─── Cost policy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hardcoded free-only: the gateway calls only the models listed in
# src/lib/free-model-catalog.ts. Allowlist / paid-override env vars are ignored.

# ─── Database / cache ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docker compose reads POSTGRES_PASSWORD and DATABASE_URL from .env (not .env.local)
# — put these two lines in .env before `docker compose up`:
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<random>
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://bcai:<same-password>@postgres:5432/bcairouter
# Outside compose (next dev / next start) set DATABASE_URL here instead; compose maps
# Postgres to localhost:5434 and Redis to localhost:6382.
# DATABASE_URL=
# REDIS_URL=

# ─── Worker ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 0 = do not start the background worker on boot.
# WORKER_AUTOSTART=
